---
import ServicePage from '../../components/services/ServicePage.astro';
import { SERVICES } from '../../data/site';

export const prerender = true;

const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/hire/ai-automation';
const svc = SERVICES[3];

const FAQ = [
  {
    q: 'What should we automate first?',
    a: "The task your team repeats most and complains about loudest. Usually that's lead intake into the CRM, follow-ups that depend on someone remembering, or a weekly report someone builds by hand. Show me that task, and I'll map it and price it.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Do we need AI, or a normal workflow?',
    a: 'Often a normal workflow. If the steps never change, plain automation is cheaper and easier to trust. I add AI when the input is messy, a decision is needed or a person should review a draft.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can we start small?',
    a: 'Yes. Start with one build. If it pays off, we plan the next one or move to a monthly arrangement.',
  },
];
---
<ServicePage
  title="Hire an AI Automation Specialist | Neil Busque"
  description="Hire Neil Busque to automate lead handling, follow-up, reporting, CRM upkeep and repetitive operations with n8n, Zapier, GHL and AI agents."
  canonical={canonical}
  active="hire"
  heading="Automate the **busywork** with AI."
  lead="I turn repeated manual work into workflows your team can see, understand and trust. Some use AI. Many don't need it."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
    { name: 'Hire', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/hire' },
    { name: 'AI Automation', url: canonical },
  ]}
  backLabel="When to hire me"
  topic="hiring for AI automation"
  artSeed="hire-ai-automation"
  artPalette="paper"
  summary={{ items: svc.items, facts: svc.facts }}
  related={['one-click-client-onboarding', 'meeting-notes-to-tasks']}
  relatedPalettes={['mist', 'navy']}
  faq={FAQ}
  service={{
    name: 'AI Automation Specialist',
    serviceType: ['AI automation', 'Workflow automation', 'Business process automation', 'CRM automation'],
    areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  }}
>
  <h2>What I automate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Leads.</strong> Capture, enrich, route and follow up automatically, so nothing sits and goes cold.</li>
    <li><strong>Follow-up and nurture.</strong> Timely sequences across email and SMS, triggered by what people actually do.</li>
    <li><strong>Ops and admin.</strong> Data entry, reporting, CRM cleanup and the handoffs that eat your team's hours.</li>
    <li><strong>Content and research.</strong> AI agents that draft, summarize and pull information together on a schedule.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Plain automation vs AI agents</h2>
  <p>When the steps never change, I build a normal workflow because it's cheaper and more predictable. I add an agent when the task involves messy input, a judgment call or a draft a person should review. Here is <a href="/guides/build-ai-agent-claude-code">how those agents work</a>.</p>

  <h2>Work you can check</h2>
  <p>At a marketing agency I built more than 20 production n8n workflows across more than 10 client accounts, plus one-click client onboarding that cut a 30-day process to 7. In 2026 I shipped more than 40 apps, agents and automations. See <a href="/work">the work</a> before we talk.</p>

  <h2>Let's find your time sinks</h2>
  <p>Tell me where your team loses hours. Message me on WhatsApp, email <a href="mailto:busqueneil@gmail.com">busqueneil@gmail.com</a> or connect on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/neilbusque/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>. Want the engineering side instead? See <a href="/hire/ai-engineer">hiring an AI engineer</a>, or the full list of <a href="/services/ai-automation-services">AI automation services</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
